    'Remote Working Study',
    'interpreting_info'::dm_question_type,
    'A management consultancy reports that teams who adopted fully remote working in 2023 saw a 12% rise in self-reported productivity. Critics note the same teams also reported higher rates of burnout and that the productivity measure relied on self-assessment rather than objective output metrics. The consultancy acknowledges these limitations but argues the results still support remote working.',
