    'Clinic Waiting Chairs',
    'logic_puzzle'::dm_question_type,
    'Six patients wait in a row of six chairs numbered 1 to 6 from left to right. The patients are Finn, Gita, Hugo, Isla, Jo, and Kai. Gita sits in chair 4. Hugo sits immediately to the left of Gita. Kai sits three chairs to the left of Jo. Finn sits in chair 6.

Who sits in chair 5?',
    NULL,
    NULL,
    'C',
    'Gita is in chair 4 and Hugo is immediately to her left in chair 3. Finn is in chair 6. That leaves Isla, Jo, and Kai for chairs 1, 2, and 5. Kai is three chairs left of Jo, so Kai = Jo − 3. The only possibility in the remaining chairs is Kai = 2, Jo = 5 — which leaves Isla in chair 1.',
    249,
    'normal',
